Where two independent formalizations of the same book item disagree in mathematical **content**, at least one is unfaithful to the book. A compiler cannot see this: a statement over `ℝ` where the book says `ℝᵈ`, a dropped `d ≥ 1`, a weakened conclusion — all typecheck. That is the entire point of the exercise.

